---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy | PhotoEditingPrompt.com" desc="How PhotoEditingPrompt.com handles data: no accounts, no photo uploads, and what is stored in your browser.">
  <div class="narrow">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › Privacy Policy</nav>
    <h1 class="page-title" style="font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,44px);margin:28px 0 20px">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Last updated: 23 November 2026.</p>
      <p>This policy explains what {SITE.name} (<a class="link" href="/">{SITE.domain}</a>, "we", "us") collects, uses and shares when you use our website. We are an independent project run from India. We have kept data collection as small as we can, and this page says exactly what that means.</p>
      <h2>1. Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>There are no accounts, no sign-up, no comments and no forms on the site.</li>
        <li>We do not ask for your name, email address, phone number, location or photos.</li>
        <li>Your photos never pass through this site. You upload them yourself to ChatGPT or Gemini.</li>
        <li>We do not sell personal data and we do not run advertising or tracking cookies at this time.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>2. Information stored in your browser</h2>
      <p>A few small settings are saved only in your own browser, on your own device. We never receive them: your light or dark theme, your language choice, and the prompts you save with the heart button (your "Saved" list). Clearing this site's data in your browser settings removes them.</p>
      <h2>3. Hosting and server logs</h2>
      <p>The website is delivered through Cloudflare. Like most hosts, Cloudflare may record standard technical information when a page is requested, such as your IP address, browser and device type, the page requested and the time, to keep the site secure and working. We use this only for security and reliability, not to identify or profile individual visitors. Cloudflare acts under its own <a class="link" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      <h2>4. Analytics, cookies and advertising</h2>
      <p>At the time of the last update this site does not use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies. If we add any of these (for example Google Analytics, or Google AdSense advertising), we will update this page first, say which service is used and what it collects, and show a consent choice where the law requires one.</p>
      <h2>5. Links to other websites and AI tools</h2>
      <p>Prompt pages link to tools such as ChatGPT, Google Gemini and Pinterest. When you follow those links, or paste a prompt and upload a photo there, the other company's terms and privacy policy apply, not ours. We do not control what they collect or how they use it. Please read their policies before uploading photos of yourself or other people.</p>
      <h2>6. The people in our example pictures</h2>
      <p>The faces in our before and after examples are AI-generated characters, not real people.</p>
      <h2>7. Children</h2>
      <p>The site is for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children. If you believe a child has sent us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>
      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Because we do not collect personal data through the site, there is normally nothing for us to access, correct or delete. Depending on where you live (for example India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, or the GDPR in Europe and the UK), you may have rights over personal data held about you. To ask a question or make a request, email us and we will respond within 30 days.</p>
      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>The site is served over HTTPS. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but because we hold so little data, there is very little to expose.</p>
      <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The "last updated" date at the top shows the latest version. Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the updated policy.</p>
      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or requests about privacy: <a class="link" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. You can also use our <a class="link" href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
